 "_note": "Kindergarten \"Words and Sentences\" (English literacy year, Part 12.3; types/_shared/sentences-k.js). `pics`: the library picture of a word (colour themes only, a picture a kindergartner names with that word; every action picture SHOWS the action being done). `sort`: `naming` words (animals and things, never a word that is also a verb a kindergartner uses), `action` words (pictures of a person doing it), `words` the short words of the word cards of level 3 (`can`: the actions each animal can do, for the sample of \"The ___ can ___.\"). `capitals`: `three` (three words) and `long` (four or five words) correct sentences; no names, no capital inside except the word I; the first letter is a capital I or a letter whose small form looks unlike its capital (never c o s u v w x y z k p, never l: a small l looks like a capital I). `marks`: sentences without their end mark, `listen` (the teacher reads, level 1) and `read` (a kindergartner reads them: only the words of READ_WORDS in the factory and the pictured noun), each telling or asking and naming its picture; `short` the read sentences that stand on ONE line of a level-3 strip of Telling or Asking? (22 px, beside a 72 px box; checked by the factory); `write` a picture with a sample telling and asking sentence. `longer`: `cues` the four pictures that tell where or when (sun, moon, rain, snow) and the words they add; `items` a short sentence that says what its picture shows, and the cues that fit it. `find` (Find the Action Word): `people` pictured people standing still (naming words), `shownIn` the things an action picture shows (never in the same row), `actWords` and `nameWords` short words a kindergartner reads (no naming word that is also a verb), `sentences` with one naming word (/n) and one action word (/a), only words of FIND_WORDS in the factory, and the worked `example`.",
